low income, more time.

573
00:19:42,827 --> 00:19:44,777
Car wash: high cost,

574
00:19:44,777 --> 00:19:47,019
high income, high risk.

575
00:19:47,199 --> 00:19:48,898
Storage: high cost,

576
00:19:48,898 --> 00:19:51,761
steady income, real estate risk.

577
00:19:52,112 --> 00:19:52,994
Let's compare.

578
00:19:53,174 --> 00:19:56,068
Vending: a few thousand dollars to start,

579
00:19:56,068 --> 00:19:57,833
small income per machine,

580
00:19:57,833 --> 00:19:59,315
real time commitment,

581
00:19:59,315 --> 00:20:01,080
and low risk per machine.

582
00:20:01,260 --> 00:20:03,589
Car wash: millions to build,

583
00:20:03,589 --> 00:20:06,915
large revenue, heavy debt and high fixed

584
00:20:06,915 --> 00:20:07,414
costs.

585
00:20:07,594 --> 00:20:10,874
Storage: hundreds of thousands to millions,

586
00:20:10,874 --> 00:20:13,620
steady income, relatively low labor,

587
00:20:13,620 --> 00:20:15,755
and real estate market risk.

588
00:20:16,106 --> 00:20:17,243
Notice something.

589
00:20:17,423 --> 00:20:19,343
None of them is truly passive at

590
00:20:19,343 --> 00:20:19,943
the start.

591
00:20:20,123 --> 00:20:22,387
Vending requires your time every week.

592
00:20:22,567 --> 00:20:26,038
Car washes require active management and marketing.

593
00:20:26,218 --> 00:20:28,042
Storage requires management,

594
00:20:28,042 --> 00:20:29,411
even if it's lighter.

595
00:20:29,591 --> 00:20:32,413
Passive income usually means you've paid someone

596
00:20:32,413 --> 00:20:33,589
else to do the work,

597
00:20:33,589 --> 00:20:35,588
and that payment comes out of your

598
00:20:35,588 --> 00:20:35,999
profit.

599
00:20:36,350 --> 00:20:38,903
These three aren't the only businesses sold

600
00:20:38,903 --> 00:20:39,972
as passive income.

601
00:20:40,152 --> 00:20:41,888
Here's a quick look at a few

602
00:20:41,888 --> 00:20:43,623
others, using the same lens.

603
00:20:43,974 --> 00:20:44,926
Laundromats.

604
00:20:45,106 --> 00:20:47,317
Steady demand and card payments,

605
00:20:47,317 --> 00:20:49,183
but equipment is expensive,

606
00:20:49,183 --> 00:20:50,911
leases matter enormously,

607
00:20:50,911 --> 00:20:53,260
and someone has to handle repairs,

608
00:20:53,260 --> 00:20:55,264
cleaning and customer issues.

609
00:20:55,444 --> 00:20:56,118
ATMs.

610
00:20:56,298 --> 00:20:58,412
Low cost machines that earn a fee

611
00:20:58,412 --> 00:21:00,783
per withdrawal, but cash use has been

612
00:21:00,783 --> 00:21:03,538
declining, and you need great locations and

613
00:21:03,538 --> 00:21:04,947
reliable cash loading.

614
00:21:05,297 --> 00:21:06,341
Parking lots.

615
00:21:06,521 --> 00:21:07,923
Simple in concept,

616
00:21:07,923 --> 00:21:09,870
with low operating costs,

617
00:21:09,870 --> 00:21:12,986
but land is expensive and demand depends

618
00:21:12,986 --> 00:21:14,310
on what's nearby,

619
00:21:14,310 --> 00:21:17,737
like offices, stadiums or downtown activity.

620
00:21:17,917 --> 00:21:18,776
Billboards.

621
00:21:18,956 --> 00:21:20,781
Can earn steady lease income,

622
00:21:20,781 --> 00:21:22,921
but permits are often hard to get,

623
00:21:22,921 --> 00:21:25,249
and you need advertisers to keep them

624
00:21:25,249 --> 00:21:25,690
rented.

625
00:21:26,040 --> 00:21:28,327
The same pattern shows up every time.

626
00:21:28,507 --> 00:21:30,439
The more passive a business is,

627
00:21:30,439 --> 00:21:32,746
the more capital it usually requires,

628
00:21:32,746 --> 00:21:34,866
and the more the returns depend on

629
00:21:34,866 --> 00:21:36,425
location and competition.

630
00:21:36,605 --> 00:21:38,684
The cheaper and easier the entry,

631
00:21:38,684 --> 00:21:40,448
the more of your own time it

632
00:21:40,448 --> 00:21:41,330
usually takes.

633
00:21:41,510 --> 00:21:42,964
There's no free lunch,

634
00:21:42,964 --> 00:21:45,344
only different trades between money,

635
00:21:45,344 --> 00:21:46,270
time and risk.

636
00:21:46,620 --> 00:21:48,001
Let's make this practical.

637
00:21:48,181 --> 00:21:51,014
Here's how these businesses might fit different

638
00:21:51,014 --> 00:21:54,088
budgets, keeping your emergency fund and retirement

639
00:21:54,088 --> 00:21:55,112
savings separate.

640
00:21:55,463 --> 00:21:57,184
With ten thousand dollars,

641
00:21:57,184 --> 00:21:58,574
vending is realistic.

642
00:21:58,754 --> 00:22:01,320
Two or three used machines in good

643
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:04,414
locations, plus a cushion for repairs and

644
00:22:04,414 --> 00:22:05,093
products.

645
00:22:05,273 --> 00:22:07,528
You'll learn the basics of locations,

646
00:22:07,528 --> 00:22:08,990
inventory and customers,

647
00:22:08,990 --> 00:22:11,245
and you'll find out whether you enjoy

648
00:22:11,245 --> 00:22:13,926
the work, all without risking your financial

649
00:22:13,926 --> 00:22:14,596
foundation.

650
00:22:14,946 --> 00:22:17,163
With one hundred thousand dollars,

651
00:22:17,163 --> 00:22:18,533
more options open up.

652
00:22:18,713 --> 00:22:20,347
A larger vending route,

653
00:22:20,347 --> 00:22:22,549
a small micro market operation,

654
00:22:22,549 --> 00:22:24,538
or a down payment on a small

655
00:22:24,538 --> 00:22:27,237
self service car wash or rural storage

656
00:22:27,237 --> 00:22:28,941
facility with financing.

657
00:22:29,121 --> 00:22:30,006
At this level,

658
00:22:30,006 --> 00:22:33,038
partnering with an experienced operator can make

659
00:22:33,038 --> 00:22:36,575
sense, and professional due diligence becomes essential.

660
00:22:36,925 --> 00:22:39,022
With a million dollars or more,

661
00:22:39,022 --> 00:22:42,405
typically through partnerships or investor groups,

662
00:22:42,405 --> 00:22:45,652
express car washes and larger storage facilities

663
00:22:45,652 --> 00:22:46,735
become possible.

664
00:22:46,915 --> 00:22:47,752
At this scale,

665
00:22:47,752 --> 00:22:50,144
you're running or investing in a serious

666
00:22:50,144 --> 00:22:51,759
business with serious debt,

667
00:22:51,759 --> 00:22:54,929
and experienced management matters more than anything

668
00:22:54,929 --> 00:22:55,228
else.

669
00:22:55,408 --> 00:22:58,022
Many people at this level invest alongside

670
00:22:58,022 --> 00:23:01,445
professional operators rather than running the business

671
00:23:01,445 --> 00:23:02,130
themselves.

672
00:23:02,480 --> 00:23:03,767
And with any budget,

673
00:23:03,767 --> 00:23:06,021
the index fund is always an option.

674
00:23:06,201 --> 00:23:07,961
It requires no time,

675
00:23:07,961 --> 00:23:10,427
no locations and no repairs.

676
00:23:10,607 --> 00:23:12,889
Any business you choose should offer a

677
00:23:12,889 --> 00:23:14,991
clear advantage over that baseline,

678
00:23:14,991 --> 00:23:16,852
in return, in control or in the

679
00:23:16,852 --> 00:23:18,954
satisfaction of building something.

680
00:23:19,134 --> 00:23:20,010
If it doesn't,

681
00:23:20,010 --> 00:23:22,075
the boring fund may be the better

682
00:23:22,075 --> 00:23:22,513
choice.

683
00:23:22,863 --> 00:23:24,858
Let's imagine three investors,

684
00:23:24,858 --> 00:23:27,054
each with fifty thousand dollars.

685
00:23:27,234 --> 00:23:29,647
The first buys ten vending machines from

686
00:23:29,647 --> 00:23:31,820
a company promising great locations.

687
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:33,968
The locations turn out to be weak,

688
00:23:33,968 --> 00:23:35,935
and half the machines barely sell.

689
00:23:36,115 --> 00:23:38,794
After a year of driving around restocking,

690
00:23:38,794 --> 00:23:40,707
he moves the machines himself,

691
00:23:40,707 --> 00:23:41,918
finds better spots,

692
00:23:41,918 --> 00:23:44,660
and finally starts earning a modest profit.

693
00:23:44,840 --> 00:23:48,149
Lesson: never outsource location selection.

694
00:23:48,500 --> 00:23:51,515
The second partners with an experienced operator

695
00:23:51,515 --> 00:23:53,463
to buy a self service car wash,

696
00:23:53,463 --> 00:23:55,788
putting in her fifty thousand as part

697
00:23:55,788 --> 00:23:57,044
of the down payment.

698
00:23:57,224 --> 00:23:59,048
The operator runs the wash,

699
00:23:59,048 --> 00:24:01,142
and she receives a share of the

700
00:24:01,142 --> 00:24:01,683
profits.

701
00:24:01,863 --> 00:24:02,729
It works well,

702
00:24:02,729 --> 00:24:04,833
because she chose a partner with a

703
00:24:04,833 --> 00:24:07,122
track record and a written agreement.

704
00:24:07,302 --> 00:24:10,238
Lesson: partners can make big deals possible,

705
00:24:10,238 --> 00:24:11,934
but choose them carefully.

706
00:24:12,285 --> 00:24:14,636
The third keeps the fifty thousand in

707
00:24:14,636 --> 00:24:17,052
an index fund while he studies storage

708
00:24:17,052 --> 00:24:17,942
for two years,

709
00:24:17,942 --> 00:24:19,912
analyzing dozens of facilities.

710
00:24:20,092 --> 00:24:22,275
When he finally buys a small rural

711
00:24:22,275 --> 00:24:23,816
facility with financing,

712
00:24:23,816 --> 00:24:25,934
he knows exactly what a good deal

713
00:24:25,934 --> 00:24:26,640
looks like.

714
00:24:26,820 --> 00:24:30,594
Lesson: patience and preparation are investments too.

715
00:24:30,944 --> 00:24:31,872
Mistake one.

716
00:24:32,052 --> 00:24:35,663
Believing projected numbers instead of real ones.

717
00:24:35,843 --> 00:24:39,105
Sellers and promoters show best case projections.

718
00:24:39,285 --> 00:24:40,911
Ask for actual records.

719
00:24:41,091 --> 00:24:42,182
Mistake two.

720
00:24:42,362 --> 00:24:43,837
Underestimating your time.

721
00:24:44,017 --> 00:24:46,964
Even the most passive businesses need oversight,

722
00:24:46,964 --> 00:24:47,762
and early on,

723
00:24:47,762 --> 00:24:49,113
they need a lot of it.

724
00:24:49,464 --> 00:24:50,532
Mistake three.

725
00:24:50,712 --> 00:24:51,594
Too much debt.

726
00:24:51,774 --> 00:24:54,513
High fixed costs plus heavy loans leave

727
00:24:54,513 --> 00:24:56,128
no room for a bad year.

728
00:24:56,308 --> 00:24:57,341
Mistake four.

729
00:24:57,521 --> 00:24:58,949
Ignoring competition.

730
00:24:59,129 --> 00:25:01,665
Check for new facilities or washes being

731
00:25:01,665 --> 00:25:03,567
planned nearby before you buy,

732
00:25:03,567 --> 00:25:06,546
using local planning records and simply driving

733
00:25:06,546 --> 00:25:07,117
the area.

734
00:25:07,467 --> 00:25:08,639
And mistake five.

735
00:25:08,819 --> 00:25:10,665
Putting everything into one deal.

736
00:25:10,845 --> 00:25:12,450
Keep your emergency fund,

737
00:25:12,450 --> 00:25:14,376
keep investing for retirement,

738
00:25:14,376 --> 00:25:16,752
and never risk money you can't afford

739
00:25:16,752 --> 00:25:17,265
to lose.

740
00:25:17,445 --> 00:25:20,453
Diversification protects you from the one bad

741
00:25:20,453 --> 00:25:23,060
location or the one new competitor that

742
00:25:23,060 --> 00:25:24,330
changes everything.

743
00:25:24,681 --> 00:25:26,190
Now, three angles.

744
00:25:26,370 --> 00:25:27,821
First, the numbers.

745
00:25:28,001 --> 00:25:30,408
How do these compare to simply investing

746
00:25:30,408 --> 00:25:31,612
in the stock market?

747
00:25:31,962 --> 00:25:34,017
Say you have fifty thousand dollars.

748
00:25:34,197 --> 00:25:35,592
In a broad index fund,

749
00:25:35,592 --> 00:25:38,573
at an illustrative seven percent average yearly

750
00:25:38,573 --> 00:25:40,983
return, that might grow by about three

751
00:25:40,983 --> 00:25:43,457
thousand five hundred dollars a year on

752
00:25:43,457 --> 00:25:45,423
average, with no time required,

753
00:25:45,423 --> 00:25:47,072
though with ups and downs.

754
00:25:47,252 --> 00:25:48,390
That's your baseline.

755
00:25:48,570 --> 00:25:50,672
Any business should beat it by enough

756
00:25:50,672 --> 00:25:52,320
to justify the time and risk.

757
00:25:52,670 --> 00:25:55,778
With fifty thousand dollars in vending machines,

758
00:25:55,778 --> 00:25:58,174
maybe twelve machines in our example,

759
00:25:58,174 --> 00:26:01,088
you might earn around twenty thousand dollars

760
00:26:01,088 --> 00:26:03,678
a year before vehicle costs and repairs,

761
00:26:03,678 --> 00:26:05,168
but with a day or two a

762
00:26:05,168 --> 00:26:06,009
week of work.

763
00:26:06,189 --> 00:26:08,102
That's a much higher return on money,

764
00:26:08,102 --> 00:26:09,756
but much of it is really payment

765
00:26:09,756 --> 00:26:10,532
for your labor.

766
00:26:10,882 --> 00:26:13,298
With fifty thousand dollars as a down

767
00:26:13,298 --> 00:26:15,454
payment, you might be able to buy

768
00:26:15,454 --> 00:26:17,674
into a small storage facility or a

769
00:26:17,674 --> 00:26:20,091
self service car wash with financing,

770
00:26:20,091 --> 00:26:21,528
depending on the deal.

771
00:26:21,708 --> 00:26:23,074
That uses leverage,

772
00:26:23,074 --> 00:26:25,016
which can multiply returns,

773
00:26:25,016 --> 00:26:26,166
but also losses.

774
00:26:26,346 --> 00:26:29,044
The question is always whether the extra

775
00:26:29,044 --> 00:26:31,338
return is worth the extra risk and

776
00:26:31,338 --> 00:26:31,675
work.

777
00:26:32,025 --> 00:26:33,627
Taxes also matter.

778
00:26:33,807 --> 00:26:37,342
Equipment and buildings can often be depreciated,

779
00:26:37,342 --> 00:26:39,723
which means part of their cost is

780
00:26:39,723 --> 00:26:42,537
deducted from taxable income over time.

781
00:26:42,717 --> 00:26:44,889
That can make the after tax returns

782
00:26:44,889 --> 00:26:47,370
of these businesses look better than the

783
00:26:47,370 --> 00:26:48,859
pre tax numbers suggest.

784
00:26:49,039 --> 00:26:51,296
But depreciation rules are complex,

785
00:26:51,296 --> 00:26:53,488
and they can create taxes when you

786
00:26:53,488 --> 00:26:53,811
sell.

787
00:26:53,991 --> 00:26:55,896
This is exactly the kind of thing

788
00:26:55,896 --> 00:26:58,032
to plan with an accountant before you

789
00:26:58,032 --> 00:26:58,263
buy.

790
00:26:58,614 --> 00:26:59,182
The lesson.

791
00:26:59,362 --> 00:27:01,437
Separate your return into two parts:

792
00:27:01,437 --> 00:27:03,511
return on your money and payment for

793
00:27:03,511 --> 00:27:04,088
your time.

794
00:27:04,268 --> 00:27:06,854
A business that pays thirty percent but

795
00:27:06,854 --> 00:27:09,440
requires twenty hours a week may really

796
00:27:09,440 --> 00:27:11,629
be a job plus a modest investment

797
00:27:11,629 --> 00:27:12,093
return.

798
00:27:12,273 --> 00:27:14,133
That's fine, but know which one you're

799
00:27:14,133 --> 00:27:14,525
getting.

800
00:27:14,876 --> 00:27:15,828
Second angle.

801
00:27:16,008 --> 00:27:17,134
The psychology.

802
00:27:17,314 --> 00:27:19,878
Why is passive income such a powerful

803
00:27:19,878 --> 00:27:21,958
idea, and why is it dangerous?

804
00:27:22,308 --> 00:27:24,295
The first reason is the dream of

805
00:27:24,295 --> 00:27:24,792
freedom.

806
00:27:24,972 --> 00:27:27,231
Earning money while you sleep sounds like

807
00:27:27,231 --> 00:27:28,885
the perfect escape from a job.

808
00:27:29,065 --> 00:27:30,240
That dream is real,

809
00:27:30,240 --> 00:27:32,281
and it can be achieved over time.

810
00:27:32,461 --> 00:27:34,655
But it's usually the result of years

811
00:27:34,655 --> 00:27:36,118
of work, not a shortcut.

812
00:27:36,298 --> 00:27:38,606
People who sell the dream often skip

813
00:27:38,606 --> 00:27:39,247
the years.

814
00:27:39,597 --> 00:27:42,000
The second reason is selective stories.

815
00:27:42,180 --> 00:27:44,405
You see the person with fifty profitable

816
00:27:44,405 --> 00:27:46,574
machines, not the hundreds who bought a

817
00:27:46,574 --> 00:27:48,577
machine that sits in a bad location.

818
00:27:48,757 --> 00:27:50,655
You see the car wash owner with

819
00:27:50,655 --> 00:27:51,940
thousands of members,

820
00:27:51,940 --> 00:27:53,838
not the one who can't cover the

821
00:27:53,838 --> 00:27:54,144
loan.

822
00:27:54,324 --> 00:27:57,589
Survivorship bias makes these businesses look easier

823
00:27:57,589 --> 00:27:58,469
than they are.

824
00:27:58,818 --> 00:28:00,694
The third reason is that the gurus

825
00:28:00,694 --> 00:28:01,686
profit either way.

826
00:28:01,866 --> 00:28:05,082
Many passive income promoters make money by

827
00:28:05,082 --> 00:28:07,027
selling courses, machines,

828
00:28:07,027 --> 00:28:08,672
coaching or locations,

829
00:28:08,672 --> 00:28:11,514
whether or not your business succeeds.

830
00:28:11,694 --> 00:28:14,016
That doesn't mean everything they say is

831
00:28:14,016 --> 00:28:16,164
false, but it means you should verify

832
00:28:16,164 --> 00:28:17,789
their numbers independently.

833
00:28:18,139 --> 00:28:20,541
The fourth reason is that we underestimate

834
00:28:20,541 --> 00:28:21,228
maintenance.

835
00:28:21,408 --> 00:28:23,779
When you picture owning a machine or

836
00:28:23,779 --> 00:28:26,083
a building, you picture the income,

837
00:28:26,083 --> 00:28:28,191
not the broken coin slot at nine

838
00:28:28,191 --> 00:28:30,298
at night, the clogged drain in a

839
00:28:30,298 --> 00:28:32,603
wash bay, or the tenant who stopped

840
00:28:32,603 --> 00:28:33,064
paying.

841
00:28:33,244 --> 00:28:35,445
Every physical asset needs care,

842
00:28:35,445 --> 00:28:37,784
and that care costs time or money.

843
00:28:38,134 --> 00:28:40,063
And the fifth reason is that easy

844
00:28:40,063 --> 00:28:41,408
feels better than hard.

845
00:28:41,588 --> 00:28:44,100
A video that says passive income is

846
00:28:44,100 --> 00:28:46,685
simple gets more views than one that

847
00:28:46,685 --> 00:28:49,773
explains depreciation, churn and cap rates.

848
00:28:49,953 --> 00:28:52,013
That's why this video exists:

849
00:28:52,013 --> 00:28:54,642
the boring details are where the real

850
00:28:54,642 --> 00:28:55,850
money is decided.

851
00:28:56,200 --> 00:28:56,909
The takeaway.

852
00:28:57,089 --> 00:28:58,562
Passive income is real,

853
00:28:58,562 --> 00:29:00,548
but it's usually earned slowly.

854
00:29:00,728 --> 00:29:03,371
Treat any promise of easy passive income

855
00:29:03,371 --> 00:29:05,617
as a reason to ask more questions,

856
00:29:05,617 --> 00:29:06,278
not fewer.

857
00:29:06,627 --> 00:29:08,011
You can learn a lot about a

858
00:29:08,011 --> 00:29:10,215
business before anyone shows you the books.

859
00:29:10,395 --> 00:29:11,789
For a vending machine,

860
00:29:11,789 --> 00:29:13,943
count how many people pass by each

861
00:29:13,943 --> 00:29:15,654
day and how long they wait.

862
00:29:15,834 --> 00:29:16,870
For a car wash,

863
00:29:16,870 --> 00:29:19,217
sit across the street on a weekday

864
00:29:19,217 --> 00:29:21,496
and a Saturday and count cars per

865
00:29:21,496 --> 00:29:24,257
hour, then check the membership price on

866
00:29:24,257 --> 00:29:24,878
the sign.

867
00:29:25,058 --> 00:29:27,581
For storage, call as a customer and

868
00:29:27,581 --> 00:29:30,247
ask what sizes are available and what

869
00:29:30,247 --> 00:29:30,968
they cost.

870
00:29:31,318 --> 00:29:32,513
Then do rough math.

871
00:29:32,693 --> 00:29:35,281
Cars per hour times hours open times

872
00:29:35,281 --> 00:29:37,869
average price gives a rough sense of

873
00:29:37,869 --> 00:29:39,090
a wash's revenue.

874
00:29:39,270 --> 00:29:42,539
Units available, compared with the total number

875
00:29:42,539 --> 00:29:44,764
of units, gives a rough sense of

876
00:29:44,764 --> 00:29:46,016
storage occupancy.

877
00:29:46,196 --> 00:29:48,049
These estimates won't be exact,

878
00:29:48,049 --> 00:29:49,782
but they help you spot when a

879
00:29:49,782 --> 00:29:51,934
seller's numbers seem too good to be

880
00:29:51,934 --> 00:29:52,233
true.

881
00:29:52,582 --> 00:29:54,603
Finally, check the competition.

882
00:29:54,783 --> 00:29:57,694
Search maps for every vending operator,

883
00:29:57,694 --> 00:30:00,456
car wash or storage facility within a

884
00:30:00,456 --> 00:30:01,203
few miles.

885
00:30:01,383 --> 00:30:03,110
Read reviews, compare prices,

886
00:30:03,110 --> 00:30:05,374
and look at local planning records for

887
00:30:05,374 --> 00:30:06,863
anything new being built.

888
00:30:07,043 --> 00:30:08,918
A deal that looks great today can

889
00:30:08,918 --> 00:30:11,248
look very different when a new competitor

890
00:30:11,248 --> 00:30:12,952
opens down the road next year.

891
00:30:13,302 --> 00:30:14,162
Third angle.

892
00:30:14,342 --> 00:30:15,143
The playbook.

893
00:30:15,323 --> 00:30:16,964
How do you decide whether any of

894
00:30:16,964 --> 00:30:18,144
these is right for you?

895
00:30:18,494 --> 00:30:19,237
Question one.

896
00:30:19,417 --> 00:30:21,587
How much capital can I risk without

897
00:30:21,587 --> 00:30:24,130
touching my emergency fund or retirement?

898
00:30:24,310 --> 00:30:26,481
That decides which of the three is

899
00:30:26,481 --> 00:30:27,375
even possible.

900
00:30:27,555 --> 00:30:28,449
Question two.

901
00:30:28,629 --> 00:30:30,224
How much time can I give each

902
00:30:30,224 --> 00:30:30,498
week?

903
00:30:30,678 --> 00:30:32,606
Vending needs regular time.

904
00:30:32,786 --> 00:30:35,084
Car washes need active management.

905
00:30:35,264 --> 00:30:36,698
Storage can be lighter,

906
00:30:36,698 --> 00:30:38,318
especially with a manager.

907
00:30:38,668 --> 00:30:39,794
Question three.

908
00:30:39,974 --> 00:30:42,005
Do I understand the local market?

909
00:30:42,185 --> 00:30:44,679
Visit competitors, count machines,

910
00:30:44,679 --> 00:30:46,219
washes or facilities,

911
00:30:46,219 --> 00:30:48,199
check prices and occupancy,

912
00:30:48,199 --> 00:30:49,593
and talk to owners.

913
00:30:49,773 --> 00:30:50,667
Question four.

914
00:30:50,847 --> 00:30:52,669
Have I seen real numbers?

915
00:30:52,849 --> 00:30:54,050
Ask for tax returns,

916
00:30:54,050 --> 00:30:56,332
bank statements and occupancy reports,

917
00:30:56,332 --> 00:30:58,434
and have an accountant review them.

918
00:30:58,784 --> 00:30:59,759
Question five.

919
00:30:59,939 --> 00:31:01,750
What happens if things go wrong?

920
00:31:01,930 --> 00:31:03,233
Run a stress test:

921
00:31:03,233 --> 00:31:05,913
what if revenue falls twenty percent,

922
00:31:05,913 --> 00:31:07,144
a machine breaks,

923
00:31:07,144 --> 00:31:09,244
or a competitor opens nearby?

924
00:31:09,424 --> 00:31:11,209
If the investment still works,

925
00:31:11,209 --> 00:31:12,934
or at least doesn't sink you,

926
00:31:12,934 --> 00:31:15,194
you may have found a good opportunity.

927
00:31:15,545 --> 00:31:16,798
A practical path.

928
00:31:16,978 --> 00:31:19,567
Many people start with vending to learn

929
00:31:19,567 --> 00:31:21,492
the basics with little money,

930
00:31:21,492 --> 00:31:24,081
keep investing in index funds for their

931
00:31:24,081 --> 00:31:26,936
foundation, and only later move into larger

932
00:31:26,936 --> 00:31:29,525
investments like storage or car washes,

933
00:31:29,525 --> 00:31:30,852
often with partners.

934
00:31:31,032 --> 00:31:32,929
Start small, learn,

935
00:31:32,929 --> 00:31:34,028
then scale.

936
00:31:34,378 --> 00:31:35,190
Question one.

937
00:31:35,370 --> 00:31:36,972
Which is best for a beginner?

938
00:31:37,152 --> 00:31:40,249
Usually vending, because it's cheap and teaches

939
00:31:40,249 --> 00:31:42,621
the basics, though it requires time.

940
00:31:42,801 --> 00:31:43,683
Question two.

941
00:31:43,863 --> 00:31:45,152
Can I finance these?

942
00:31:45,332 --> 00:31:48,551
Car washes and storage facilities are often

943
00:31:48,551 --> 00:31:50,947
financed with bank or SBA loans,

944
00:31:50,947 --> 00:31:54,840
which require down payments and personal guarantees.

945
00:31:55,020 --> 00:31:58,170
Vending machines are usually bought with cash

946
00:31:58,170 --> 00:31:59,920
or small equipment loans.

947
00:32:00,270 --> 00:32:01,268
Question three.

948
00:32:01,448 --> 00:32:03,236
Are franchises a good idea?

949
00:32:03,416 --> 00:32:06,392
Some car wash and vending franchises offer

950
00:32:06,392 --> 00:32:08,517
systems and brand recognition,

951
00:32:08,517 --> 00:32:10,997
but they charge fees and royalties.

952
00:32:11,177 --> 00:32:13,197
Compare total costs carefully.

953
00:32:13,377 --> 00:32:14,480
Question four.

954
00:32:14,660 --> 00:32:17,006
How do I find locations or deals?

955
00:32:17,186 --> 00:32:20,088
For vending, ask local businesses directly.

956
00:32:20,268 --> 00:32:22,074
For car washes and storage,

957
00:32:22,074 --> 00:32:23,746
look at business brokers,

958
00:32:23,746 --> 00:32:27,090
commercial real estate listings and owners nearing

959
00:32:27,090 --> 00:32:27,826
retirement.

960
00:32:28,177 --> 00:32:29,221
Question five.

961
00:32:29,401 --> 00:32:31,468
Can these businesses be run remotely?

962
00:32:31,648 --> 00:32:34,242
Storage facilities increasingly can,

963
00:32:34,242 --> 00:32:36,547
with online rentals and cameras.

964
00:32:36,727 --> 00:32:39,433
Car washes usually need on site staff.

965
00:32:39,613 --> 00:32:41,825
Vending needs someone to restock,

966
00:32:41,825 --> 00:32:44,373
though some owners hire route drivers.

967
00:32:44,553 --> 00:32:45,667
Question six.

968
00:32:45,847 --> 00:32:47,798
What's the biggest hidden cost?

969
00:32:47,978 --> 00:32:50,358
For vending, your time and driving.

970
00:32:50,538 --> 00:32:51,599
For car washes,

971
00:32:51,599 --> 00:32:53,510
equipment repairs and debt.

972
00:32:53,690 --> 00:32:56,531
For storage, property taxes and the cost

973
00:32:56,531 --> 00:32:57,312
of capital.

974
00:32:57,663 --> 00:32:58,649
Question seven.

975
00:32:58,829 --> 00:33:00,818
Is it better to buy one big

976
00:33:00,818 --> 00:33:02,881
asset or several small ones?

977
00:33:03,061 --> 00:33:06,576
Several small ones spread risk across locations,

978
00:33:06,576 --> 00:33:08,773
while one big one is easier to

979
00:33:08,773 --> 00:33:11,409
manage and may get better financing.

980
00:33:11,589 --> 00:33:14,683
Many investors start small and diversify,

981
00:33:14,683 --> 00:33:17,777
then consolidate as they gain experience.

982
00:33:18,127 --> 00:33:18,974
Let's recap.

983
00:33:19,154 --> 00:33:21,708
Vending machines are cheap and teach the

984
00:33:21,708 --> 00:33:24,007
basics, but need your time and great

985
00:33:24,007 --> 00:33:24,646
locations.

986
00:33:24,826 --> 00:33:27,239
Car washes can be very profitable with

987
00:33:27,239 --> 00:33:29,462
memberships, but they're expensive,

988
00:33:29,462 --> 00:33:31,176
debt heavy and competitive.

989
00:33:31,356 --> 00:33:33,192
Storage is the most passive,

990
00:33:33,192 --> 00:33:34,569
but it's real estate,

991
00:33:34,569 --> 00:33:37,126
with big capital needs and market risk.

992
00:33:37,477 --> 00:33:38,997
And the lessons for all three.

993
00:33:39,177 --> 00:33:40,997
Separate your return on money from your

994
00:33:40,997 --> 00:33:41,790
payment for time.

995
00:33:41,970 --> 00:33:43,920
Stress test every deal.

996
00:33:44,100 --> 00:33:46,085
Verify numbers independently.

997
00:33:46,265 --> 00:33:49,291
And keep your personal financial foundation strong

998
00:33:49,291 --> 00:33:50,259
while you build.

999
00:33:50,610 --> 00:33:51,678
One last thought.

1000
00:33:51,858 --> 00:33:55,077
Vending machines, car washes and storage units

1001
00:33:55,077 --> 00:33:56,757
really can build wealth.

1002
00:33:56,937 --> 00:33:58,528
Plenty of people have done it.

1003
00:33:58,708 --> 00:34:01,361
But the ones who succeed usually treat

1004
00:34:01,361 --> 00:34:03,037
them as real businesses:

1005
00:34:03,037 --> 00:34:04,643
they study the numbers,

1006
00:34:04,643 --> 00:34:06,109
pick great locations,

1007
00:34:06,109 --> 00:34:08,483
manage carefully and stay patient.

1008
00:34:08,663 --> 00:34:09,746
The passive part,

1009
00:34:09,746 --> 00:34:10,511
if it comes,

1010
00:34:10,511 --> 00:34:12,677
comes later, as a reward for doing

1011
00:34:12,677 --> 00:34:14,015
the active part well.

1012
00:34:14,366 --> 00:34:16,322
If one of these interests you,

1013
00:34:16,322 --> 00:34:17,626
start with research,

1014
00:34:17,626 --> 00:34:18,278
not money.

1015
00:34:18,458 --> 00:34:21,096
This week, visit one vending location,

1016
00:34:21,096 --> 00:34:23,595
one car wash or one storage facility

1017
00:34:23,595 --> 00:34:26,024
near you, and try to estimate their

1018
00:34:26,024 --> 00:34:28,245
numbers using today's framework.

1019
00:34:28,425 --> 00:34:30,502
Write down your guesses for revenue,

1020
00:34:30,502 --> 00:34:31,483
costs and profit,

1021
00:34:31,483 --> 00:34:33,733
then compare them with what you learned

1022
00:34:33,733 --> 00:34:34,079
today.

1023
00:34:34,259 --> 00:34:36,278
Doing this a few times trains your

1024
00:34:36,278 --> 00:34:37,882
eye faster than any course.

1025
00:34:38,062 --> 00:34:39,153
I'm Ryan Rover.

1026
00:34:39,333 --> 00:34:40,266
Run the numbers,

1027
00:34:40,266 --> 00:34:41,897
and I'll see you in the next

1028
00:34:41,897 --> 00:34:42,247
video.
